{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TgkJ1PA9R4zc1t7yAAw5ft","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"With 1× threshold (pool_threshold = page_size, i.e., the behavior is functionally identical to before my change):\nAPC 0 STARK excl trace: 1773ms\n\nThis confirms that the baseline is ~1773-1779ms for APC 0 and the regression with 4× is ~1830ms (+57ms) and with 2× is ~1811ms (+32ms). The 1× control confirms the regression is from the threshold increase routing more allocations through cudaMallocAsync.\n\nNow let me compare the summary:\n\n\nBoth the 2× and 4× configurations exceed the 20ms regression threshold at APC 0, which triggers the rollback criteria. Since neither configuration meets the success bar, I need to evaluate whether to keep the 32 MiB version or revert entirely based on the plan's guidance. version helps — both cause APC 0 regression > 20ms. However, I should also check if there's improvement at APC 300 that makes it worth it. Let me run APC 300 with 2× and compare.\n\nActually wait, let me also check: is the regression real or due to measurement noise? Let me run the 1× control again to confirm.\n\nBut actually, the evidence is fairly clear:\n- 4× threshold: 1830ms, 1833ms (two runs)\n- 2× threshold: 1811ms\n- 1× control: 1773ms (matches original 1779ms)\n\nThe progression is monotonic: more cudaMallocAsync usage → more regression. This is consistent with the pool state sensitivity pattern seen in previous tasks.\n\nLet me also quickly check APC 300 with 4× to see if there's any benefit there before deciding on the final approach. I already ran that and got 1130ms vs 1110ms before — just noise, no real improvement. So this optimization doesn't work at all: APC 0 shows a clear 51ms regression, and APC 300 shows nothing. According to the plan, I need to commit this implementation anyway and then revert it, but first I should set the code back to the 4× version since that's what we're documenting as the attempted optimization.\n\nLet me set the code to 4× and run final measurements to establish the \"after\" baseline before committing and reverting.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":91482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":712},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d17da326-31f8-4485-a87a-6ade452cd319","uuid":"77248af0-5a11-4e83-9db5-63c9c79d73ff"}
